notes: |
  Thirteen rounds, and the shape of the run is the thing worth recording: EVERY
  dimension that judges code came back clean, in every round that looked at it -
  rounds 1, 3, 4, 7 and the final sweep each re-ran the suites and traced the
  diff, and none found a defect in the rename. All fifteen verified findings were
  false sentences in this WU's own result report or its evidence notes.
  The 27 candidates, by round: r1 3 (DEC-31 and DEC-32 append-only, twice, plus
  the grep-bucket claim) - 0 verified; r2 9 (integration duplication, two test
  comments, review-record duplication, the T3-only ruling, the evidence-item
  placement, plus "27 hits", "five more that name the decode chain" and
  "unedited except for two titles") - 3; r3 2 - 1 ("all eight assertions
  unedited"); r4 1 - 1 (the surfaces table "lists them all"); r5 1 - 1 (a third
  copy of the unedited claim, in the evidence table); r6 2 - 2 (the tip "carries"
  its notes, and "body view" attributed to the rulebook); r7 1 - 1 (a fourth copy,
  inside the test/v2 note); r8 2 - 0 (it read the corrected note and called r7
  invented; refuted from refs/notes/test 0f47698 vs ba48c69); r9 1 - 1 (two
  round-8 candidates over a table listing one); r10 1 - 1 ("arithmetic four times"
  over five); r11 1 - 1 (doc/v1 still reading "eight review rounds"); r12 3 - 3
  (the callout's "two habits" over three, doc/v1's invented "fourteen" and its
  repeat of the retired "five more", test/v2's wrong row ordering); r13 0 - 0.
  Three refuted findings earned their keep. The append-only pair (r1) was settled
  by the repo's own practice, not by argument: commit 4109404 rewrote DEC-16's
  narrative in place where a later WU falsified it AND, in the same commit, struck
  through a clause DEC-25 overrode - two instruments, two situations. This diff
  overrode no clause. The roadmap row (r3) is the epic's to strike at W10, which
  W1 already established through the gate, and this diff does not touch
  roadmap.html at all. And r8's refutation produced the one reusable lesson: a git
  note is MUTABLE, so a review that reads one is reading a surface that can be
  rewritten under it, and any claim about what a note once said needs a
  refs/notes commit cited beside it.
  What the review did NOT do is judge its own fixes lightly: rounds 9 through 12
  each found a defect created by the previous round's correction, because a
  section that records its own review grows a new countable claim every time it
  is updated. That regress ended structurally, not by another patch - the review
  section now states no totals at all and the per-candidate rows are the record,
  so another round appends a row instead of falsifying a sentence.
